in k8s , secretes are objects used to store sensitive information securely instead of writing them directly inside application code r yaml files.

              configmap                                                                  secret

  stores normal configuration data                                        stores sensitive data
  ex app name,port no.                                                     ex password,tokens
  data stored as plain text by default                                     data stored in base64 encoded form
  less secure                                                              more secure than configmap
  used for non sensitive info                                              used for sensitive info

  in k8s encoding is used to convert data from one format into another format for safe data transfer,store binary data as text,standardized communication
